# Pull request style

When creating or editing a GitHub PR for this repo:

## Title
- Short and operative (what changed), e.g. `Add team documentation`
- No emoji, no trailing marketing

## Body
Write lean paragraphs in operative language:

```text
Add <file or change> to <accomplish X> because <reason>.

…
```

Include a few sentences on **why this solves the problem** and **why it does not break existing behavior** (scope: docs-only, tests still pass, behavior unchanged, etc.).

## Do not include
- `Made with Cursor` or similar tool footers
- Long Test plan checklists unless the user asks
- Policy quotes, filler, or restating the entire diff

## How to pass the body
Prefer `gh pr create --body-file <path>` (or `gh pr edit --body-file`) so nothing appends extra footers.
